QuestGuidance.Register("en",53,{
[1665]="70054F3D\n1\tSearch for signs of Nidhlas and his men in Thuringwath\tNidhlas and his men might be found somewhere in Thuringwath. Mithrandir has asked you to continue ahead in search of Nidhlas and his men.\n2\tFollow the footprints deeper into Thuringwath\tThe footprints continue along the old roadway through Thuringwath. You discovered footprints on the old roadway through Thuringwath. You should follow them.\n3\tSearch Aufaltor for signs of Nidhlas and his men\tAufaltor can be found in Thuringwath. You have followed the footprints to the base of a great fane. You should search the fane for Nidhlas and his men.\n4\tExamine the slain Rangers in Aufaltor\tSlain Rangers can be found deep within Aufaltor. You have discovered a number of slain Rangers within Aufaltor. You should examine them.\n5\tExamine the heap of flesh\tYou should examine the heap of discarded flesh. You discovered the Rangers slain from bloodletting, but a heap of flesh has caught your eye. You should examine it.\n6\tReturn to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Thuringwath. You found a grisly scene at Aufaltor. You should return to Mithrandir.\n7\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found near Aufaltor in Thuringwath. You have found Mithrandir standing before a great watching-stone in Thuringwath. You should tell Mithrandir what you have found.\n",
[1666]="70064EF8\n1\tSpeak to Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth.\n",
[1667]="70064EF3\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Before the Shadow barter currency allowance.\n",
[1668]="70043B7D\n1\tGive a tasty treat to a Chetwood chicken\030Give a tasty treat to a Gloomglens pullet\030Give a tasty treat to a Kingsfell hen\030Give a tasty treat to a Lossarnach hen\030Give a tasty treat to a Rushgore bantam\tChickens can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue chickens using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1669]="7005224C\n1\tGive a tasty treat to an Oatbarton badger\030Give a tasty treat to a Gloomglens badger\030Give a tasty treat to a Lasgalen badger\030Give a tasty treat to a Thinglad badger\030Give a tasty treat to a Green Hill badger\tBadgers can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue badgers using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1670]="70052240\n1\tGive a tasty treat to a Harloeg swan\030Give a tasty treat to a Mournshaws raven\030Give a tasty treat to a Limlight dipper\030Give a tasty treat to a Gravenwood warbler\030Give a tasty treat to a Bruinen thrush\tBirds can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue birds using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1671]="7005223C\n1\tGive a tasty treat to a Rauros snapper\030Give a tasty treat to a Long Lake loggerhead\030Give a tasty treat to an Entwash slowpoke\030Give a tasty treat to a Noman-lands tortoise\030Give a tasty treat to a Dunbog cooter\tTurtles can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue turtles using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1672]="70043BBE\n1\tGive a tasty treat to a Bindbole kid\030Give a tasty treat to a Brandy Hills billy\030Give a tasty treat to a High Moor goat\030Give a tasty treat to a Hollin Ridge goat\030Give a tasty treat to a Lune River goat\tGoats can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue goats using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1673]="70052247\n1\tGive a tasty treat to a Redhorn rabbit\030Give a tasty treat to a Calembel cottontail\030Give a tasty treat to a Coomb coney\030Give a tasty treat to a Broadacres bunny\030Give a tasty treat to a Heathfells hare\tRabbits can be found all over Middle-earth. Rescue rabbits using Radagast's calming treats.\n2\tSpeak with Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should speak with Radagast.\n",
[1674]="70071A76\n1\tPick up the Mûmak Trainers' Horn\tNamâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should pick up the horn from atop the wall next to her.\n2\tGo to the Spent-lodes\tNamâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should go to the Spent-lodes in southern An Shêru.\n3\tBefriend a young mûmak using the horn\tNamâdi has asked you to use her Mûmak Trainers' Horn to train a young mûmak and bring it back to her at Khanâg Gur. You should use the horn on one of the young mûmakil.\n4\tBefriend a young mûmak using the horn\tTry once again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.\n5\tTry again to befriend a young mûmak using the horn\tTry again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.\n6\tTry again to befriend a young mûmak using the horn\tYou are finding it difficult to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.\n7\tTry once more to befriend a young mûmak using the horn\tYou are finding it very difficult to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.\n8\tTry once more to befriend a young mûmak using the horn\tYou begin to wonder if it is even possible to befriend a young mûmak. Try again to use the Mûmak Trainers' Horn on young mûmakil at the Spent-lodes, and bring one back with you to Khanâg Gur.\n9\tTalk to Namâdi at Khanâg Gur\tYou're pretty sure it is impossible to befriend a young mûmak by just using the Mûmak Trainers' Horn.\n",
[1675]="7007162E\n1\tComplete quests in Ahâba (total: 3)\tUnusâli has decided she will not trust you until you prove yourself to the Beltáni. You should complete three quests in Ahâba to prove yourself.\n2\tTalk to Unusâli\tUnusâli has heard of your work for the Beltáni and is pleased. You should talk to Unusâli in Ahâba.\n",
[1676]="70026193\n1\tAid Erchiel at Amon Môth\030Aid Lithuifin at Amon Môth\030Aid Remmenylf at Amon Môth\tThe Elves have ideas on how to help ease Longbough's pain.\n2\tTalk to Lithuifin at the Eavespires\tLithuifin is at the Eavespires. Lithuifin has a plan to drive off the giants for good.\n",
[1677]="7006AE6B\n1\tDefeat Umâr\tLocate Umâr within Harkhaphâr and defeat him.\n2\tReturn to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and present him with the journal\tReturn to Dabôr the Breaker in Hulzidâr and inform him of Umâr's demise and the recovery of the journal.\n",
[1678]="70020F04\n1\tRescue Dagoras from Lhe Lhechu\tDagoras is being held in Lhe Lhechu, south-west of Echad Dagoras. You must free Dagoras and escort him from the Dunlending camp.\n2\tTalk to Dagoras at Echad Dagoras\tDagoras ia at Echad Dagoras, north-east of Lhe Lhechu. You should speak with Dagoras at his encampment.\n",
[1679]="70062D2E\n1\tExplore the waterfall behind the bridge\030Explore the south-eastern waterfall\030Explore the eastern waterfall\030Explore the north-eastern waterfall\030Explore the north-western waterfall\030Explore the southern waterfall\tDrudwen has asked you to explore the waterfalls in and around Clegur. Clegur is in the south-west of Swanfleet.\n2\tBring the pottery to Drudwen\tYou should report back to Drudwen with the pottery and news of the skeleton you found behind the waterfalls. Drudwen is in the town of Clegur, in southern Swanfleet.\n",
[1680]="7000B695\n1\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins\030Collect Bilbo's Birthday Present\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House at Rivendell. Frodo Baggins has asked that you deliver a belated birthday present to Bilbo.\n2\tTalk to Frodo Baggins\030Collect Frodo's Birthday Present\tFrodo Baggins is in Bilbo's room on the ground floor of the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Bilbo Baggins has asked that you bring Frodo a birthday present in return.\n3\tTalk to Bilbo Baggins\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire in the Last Homely House, in Rivendell. Frodo Baggins has asked you to thank Bilbo for his gift.\n",
[1681]="70000D4A\n1\tBring the Founding Writ to Brombard Foxtail\tBrombard Foxtail is at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving. Belco Brockhouse, satisifed with your services, exhorted you to take his copy of the Founding Writ directly to Keeper Brombard Foxtail. He has no desire to see it end up in the hands of Adelard Took.\n",
[1682]="7004CE94\n1\tRemove angry scrawls (total: 10)\tYou should find angry scrawls on walls and doors throughout Dale and remove them.\n2\tReturn to Gaumar\tYou should return to Gaumar, who stands within the Great-keep in Dale.\n",
[1683]="70026C63\n1\tFind Mosco's lucky bait\030Find Mosco's fishing pole\030Find Mosco's hoe\030Find Mosco's cloak\030Find Mosco's elevenses meal\tMosco's missing goods are scattered around the Pond and the area nearby. If you read the note he gave you, perhaps there will be clues to the exact whereabouts of his gear. You should collect Mosco's missing goods and return them to him.\n2\tBring the found items to Mosco Smallburrow\tMosco Smallburrow is at the Bywater Pond, waiting for you to return with his found belongings. You should return Mosco's belongings to him.\n",
[1684]="70051396\n1\tLook out from atop the Dáinlik\tThe Dáinlik can be found in the Ironfold. You should look out over the top of the Dáinlik.\n2\tInvestigate the base of the Dáinlik\tThe Dáinlik can be found in the Ironfold. You should investigate the base of the Dáinlik.\n3\tTalk to Rísti Graver\tRísti Graver can be found atop of the Dáinlik. You should talk to Rísti Graver.\n",
[1685]="7004F91B\n1\tFind and defeat Gundabad black-arrows (total: 3)\tGundabad black-arrows can be found along the Men Angrún, especially as it nears the Rushgate. The raven told Dori that cruel archers of Gundabad have been taking ravens' feathers for their arrows. You should defeat them and take their arrows.\n2\tSearch for the lost raven near the Rushgate\tOne of Arcah's ravens can be found at the Rushgate. After speaking with the raven, Dori has learned that the other two ravens sent from Ravenhill have not returned. You should search for one of the ravens near the Rushgate.\n3\tDirect the raven to fly to Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu\tOne of Arcah's ravens can be found at the Rushgate. You have found the raven at the Rushgate. You should now follow the road to Thikil-gundu to the east and rejoin Dori and Company.\n4\tFollow the road to Thikil-gundu and and find Dori and Company\tDori can be found somewhere along the road to Thikil-gundu. The raven has flown from the Rushgate. You should now find Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu.\n5\tDeliver the raven-fletched arrows to Dori on the road to Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found on a hilltop overlooking Stánbalk, the Stone Wall of Thikil-gundu. You have found Dori and Company along the road to Thikil-gundu. You should now speak to Dori.\n6\tFind the lost raven near Thikil-gundu\tThe lost raven can be found somewhere near Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. Dori has asked you to seek the raven that flew near to Thikil-gundu.\n7\tExamine the frozen raven, but remain on guard\tThe slain, frozen raven can be found on the ground before Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You have found the frozen remains of a raven before Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You should examine it.\n8\tTalk to Dori on the road to Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found on a hilltop overlooking Stánbalk, the Stone Wall of Thikil-gundu. You have learned that one of Arcah's ravens was slain by a cold-drake. You should return to Dori.\n",
[1686]="7002EF4D\n1\tFinish helping the Rohirrim at the camp, then investigate the cave-mouth\tThe cave-mouth you discovered is south of Mansig's encampment, near where the stream flows back into the East Wall, in the western cliffs. Utlac wants you to finish helping his friends at the Rohirrim-camp in the East Wall, then investigate the cave you discovered.\n2\tTalk to the man in the cave\tYou have found a man inside the cave-system beneath the East Wall.\n",
[1687]="70052B1D\n1\tSearch the crossway to the old forest road\tThe crossway to the old forest road can be found by following the road to the north of Hultvís. Ríkmar has suggested that you begin your search for Hárskor at the crossway to the old forest road.\n2\tFind the source of the scent at the crossway\tThe source of the scent can be found somewhere around the crossway to the old forest road. You searched the crossway to the old forest road as Ríkmar suggested, but found no sign of Hárskor. However, you notice a curious scent lingering in the air.\n3\tSearch the Old Ford\tThe Old Ford can be found far to the north-west of Hultvís. You found no sign of Hárskor at the crossway, but you learned that Orcs are trapping the roads in Woodsedge. You should continue to the next location that Ríkmar marked on your map: the Old Ford.\n4\tSearch the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant\tThe road into the Beorning-lands can be found by following the road north from Hultvís. You found no sign of Hárskor or that he crossed the Old Ford. You should continue to follow the road north toward the Beorning-lands and search for Hárskor at the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant.\n5\tExamine the slain Orc\tThe slain Orc can be found on the side of the road through Woodsedge near the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant. You have discovered the mauled remains of an Orc near the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant. You should examine its corpse before continuing your search.\n6\tFollow the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant\tThe path to the ruins of Hadhodiant can be found in north-west Woodsedge. You discovered a slain Orc at the foot of the path to the ruins of Hadhodiant. Its wounds were deep and not unlike those made by a skin-changer. You should follow the path to the ruins of the old bridge and search for Hárskor.\n7\tTalk to Hárskor at the ruins of Hadhodiant\tHárskor can be found at the ruins of Hadhodiant. You have found Hárskor alive, if battle-weary, at the ruins of Hadhodiant. You should speak to him and learn what has happened.\n",
[1688]="70051397\n1\tTalk to Rísti Graver\030Talk to Aflur Smokebeard\030Complete Below the Dáinlik\030Complete Rumblings at Hammerstead\tRísti Graver can be found at the Dáinlik in the Ironfold, while Aflur Smokebeard can be found at Hammerstead in the Ironfold. You should talk to Rísti Graver and Aflur Smokebeard.\n2\tTalk to Náin\tNáin can be found in Járnfast. You should return to Náin.\n3\tInvestigate the southern mine entrance\030Investigate the eastern mine entrance\tInvestigate the entrances to the mine within Járnfast.\n4\tTalk to Náin\tNáin can be found in Járnfast. You should return to Náin.\n",
[1689]="700078E9\n1\tFind the Hanging Tree\tThe Hanging Tree sits along the river-bank south of Constable Wren's post, south-east of Combe. Ted Pickthorn's father was once a robber in the Chetwood and had purportedly garnered a significant amount of wealth. Ted believes his father's ill-gotten gains are buried at the foot of the Hanging Tree. The tree is supposed to be marked with an X.\n2\tAlthough there is no way to tell which stump was once the Hanging Tree, it would not hurt to dig near a few of the stumps in search of the treasure.\t\n3\tBring the pick-axe back to Ted Pickthorn\tTed Pickthorn can be found on the east side of Combe. Ted Pickthorn sent you to retrieve his father's loot from beneath the Hanging Tree, but you discovered that the tree, among others, was chopped down by the woodcutters of Combe. You dug at several places on the field, but found no sign of Pickthorn's buried treasure.\n",
[1690]="700479DB\n1\tEnter the enemy encampment of Dûm Boha\tThe Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills. You should seal off the maggot-hole entrances scattered around the encampment.\n2\tSeal off maggot-holes (total: 8)\tThe Haradrim encampment of Dûm Boha is located on the western slopes of the Slag-hills. You should seal off the maggot-hole entrances scattered around the encampment.\n3\tCompleted\tSealed off many of the maggot-holes in Dûm Boha.\n",
[1691]="70042E3B\n1\tTalk to Hundi at Echad Dúnann\tHundi is at the camp of Echad Dúnann, outside the Walls of Moria, in Eregion.\n",
[1692]="7002EF01\n1\tCollect the son's blanket\030Collect the daughter's dress\030Collect the husband's sickle\tThere may be remnants of Agela's family's belongings near her home in Thornhope. You should search for items once belonging to Agela's family. They might help her deal with her grief.\n2\tBring the items to Agela\tAgela is encamped outside the walls of Thornhope. You should bring the items you found to Agela.\n",
[1693]="70026C8A\n1\tReturn to the hungry cave-claw\030Collect berries (total: 5)\tYou should collect berries in the Treasure Field for the hungry cave-claw.\n",
[1694]="70044AB2\n1\tTalk to Bert Bartleby in the town of Forlaw\tBert Bartleby is by the stables in the town of Forlaw, in Wildermore. Bingo told you that Bert Bartleby wanted to have a word with you.\n2\tFind the lore-master at the west gate of Forlaw\tThe lore-master was last seen near the west-gate of Forlaw. Bert Bartleby asked you to find the lore-master that came to Forlaw and buy some potions and scrolls from him.\n3\tTalk to the guard of Forlaw at the west gate\tOne of the guards at the west gate of Forlaw has called you over to him.\n4\tTalk to Bert Bartleby in Forlaw\tBert Bartleby is near the stables of Forlaw, in Wildermore.\n5\tFind Humfrey Rumming somewhere to the west of Forlaw\tHumfrey Rumming set out from Forlaw heading west, and Bert Bartleby has asked you to track him down.\n6\tDefeat frozen efts to the west of Dunfast (total: 8)\tHumfrey Rumming caused a plague of Frozen Efts to emerge at the base of the mountains to the west of Dunfast.\n7\tTalk to Humfrey Rumming at the town of Dunfast\tHumfrey Rumming is at the abandoned town of Dunfast, in Wildermore.\n8\tBring the various sundries to Bert Bartleby in Forlaw\tBert Bartleby is by the stables in the town of Forlaw, in Wildermore. Humfrey took the money-purse given to you by Bert Bartleby and traded you some various sundries in return.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in the town of Forlaw\tBingo is in the town of Forlaw, west of the Forlaw Feasting Hall.\n",
[1695]="7000B9FC\n1\tFind someone who knows the fate of Bert, Tom, and Bill\030Find Bert, Tom, and Bill\tThe trolls that terrorized the village that Garbert's grandparents once lived in probably met their end somewhere within the wilderness of the Trollshaws. Garbert lives in a cottage along the banks of the river in Tâl Bruinen. Garbert has asked you to find the location where the three trolls of which he spoke met their end and to learn the story of their undoing.\n2\tTalk to Garbert\tGarbert lives at his cottage in Tâl Bruinen, on the banks of the river. You have learned what befell the trolls Bert, Tom, and Bill, and have visited the glade where they were turned to stone. You should return to Garbert with the news.\n",
[1696]="7004521B\n1\tTalk to Bargwen\tBargwen is located in the southern end of Ost Rimmon. Go to Bargwen and tell her of Lady Glánhar's wish to restore the banners to the walls.\n2\tGather the banners (total: 6)\tYou should gather the stored banners from the store-house in Ost Rimmon.\n3\tReturn to Bargwen\tYou should bring the banners to Bargwen, who is in the southern end of Ost Rimmon.\n4\tTake the empty bucket\tYou should take the bucket and and fill it at the well in the centre of Ost Rimmon, then bring it back to Bargwen.\n5\tFill the bucket at the well\tYou should take the bucket and and fill it at the well in the centre of Ost Rimmon, then bring it back to Bargwen.\n6\tTalk to Bargwen\tYou should talk to Bargwen, who is in the southern end of Ost Rimmon.\n7\tPick up the pile of dirty banners\030Put the banners in the bucket\tYou should put the dirty banners in the bucket of water to wash them.\n8\tWash the banners\tYou should wash the banners in the bucket of water.\n9\tTake banners out of the bucket\030Hang banners on the poles (total: 6)\tYou should place the cleaned, wet banners on the poles to dry.\n10\tYou should place the cleaned, wet banners on the poles to dry.\t\n11\tTalk to Bargwen\tBargwen is in the southern end of Ost Rimmon. You should talk to Bargwen now that the banners are washed and hung on the poles.\n12\tReturn to Lady Glánhar\tYou should return to Lady Glánhar in the centre of Ost Rimmon and tell her that the banners are ready and will be hung shortly.\n",
})
